# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  YOUR SETTINGS.  Copy this file, then fill in what you need:
#
#      cp .env.example .env
#
#  READ THIS FIRST: you need NOTHING in this file to start building.
#  `python run_once.py --drop` reads .txt files out of the drop/ folder and
#  needs no settings at all. Come back here at Step 7b.
#
#  Anything you leave blank just stays switched off. Nothing breaks.
#
#  Check what the kit can currently see, at any time:
#      python config.py
#      python preflight.py
#
#  ⚠ .env is in .gitignore and the hook blocks it. It must NEVER be committed.
#    If you ever push one by mistake, CHANGE THE PASSWORD — deleting the file
#    does not remove it from your git history.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  A · YOUR LIVE PAGE            Needed at Step 7b. This is what makes the
#                                page on the internet show your records.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your public Railway URL. Get it by running:   railway domain
# It looks like  https://my-work-log-production.up.railway.app
# No slash at the end.
SYNC_URL=

# A password you invent, right now. Any long random string — mash the keyboard.
# It stops anyone else writing records to your page.
#
# It must be THE SAME in two places:
#   1. here, in this file
#   2. on Railway:   railway variables --set SYNC_TOKEN=the-same-string
#
# If they do not match you get "HTTP 403" and your page stays empty.
SYNC_TOKEN=

# Your name at the top of the page. Optional, but it is your work log.
OWNER_NAME=my work log


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  B · YOUR MAILBOX              OPTIONAL. Skip all of this if you want.
#                                `--drop` does the same job with no mailbox.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Do not lose an hour here. If it fights you, walk away and use drop/.

# Gmail: leave as is.  Outlook/Office 365: outlook.office365.com
IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com

# The email address the transcripts arrive at.
IMAP_USER=

# ⚠ NOT your normal password. A 16-character APP PASSWORD.
#
# Where to get it (Gmail):
#   1. Your Google account needs 2-Step Verification switched on.
#   2. Go to  https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Create one. Google shows you 16 letters. Paste them below.
#   4. Spaces do not matter. You can revoke it any time.
#
# If your organisation has disabled IMAP you will get a LOGIN error.
# Tell an organiser and use drop/ instead.
IMAP_PASSWORD=

# REQUIRED if you use the mailbox. Only emails whose SUBJECT contains this
# word are ever opened.
#
# Without it the job REFUSES to run — otherwise it would read every unread
# email you have, including personal and HR mail, and mark it read. Make your
# notetaker's subject line contain this word.
SUBJECT_FILTER=transcript


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  C · TUNING                    OPTIONAL. The defaults are the right choice.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# How often schedule.py wakes up, in seconds. 300 = 5 minutes.
# Make it 60 while you are testing so you are not waiting around.
RUN_EVERY_SECONDS=300

# Which Claude model reads your transcripts.
# haiku is fast and cheap and is what today is built around. Changing this to
# a bigger model is the quickest way to hit your usage limit by 3pm.
CLAUDE_HELPER_MODEL=haiku

# Seconds to wait for Claude before giving up on one call.
CLAUDE_HELPER_TIMEOUT=120


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  D · THINGS THAT DO *NOT* GO IN THIS FILE
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  YOUR NOTION TOKEN  →  goes in  .mcp.json  , not here.
#      cp .mcp.json.example .mcp.json
#      then replace YOUR_NOTION_TOKEN inside it.
#      Get the token at  https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
#      (New integration → copy the "Internal Integration Secret",
#       then share your Notion page with that integration.)
#      .mcp.json is gitignored and hook-blocked, same as this file.
#
#  PORT  →  Railway sets this itself. Do not set it. serve.py reads it
#           automatically and falls back to 8000 on your laptop.
#
#  YOUR CLAUDE LOGIN  →  you do not need one here.
#      The job runs on YOUR LAPTOP, where you are already signed in to
#      Claude Code. That is the whole reason Step 4 has no token in it.
#
#      Only if you later run the job somewhere that has no browser to log in
#      with — a server, not your laptop — would you need a long-lived token:
#
#          claude setup-token          # prints a long token
#
#      ...and then uncomment the line below and paste it in.
#
#      ⚠ Leave it commented out otherwise. Putting a wrong or expired token
#        here overrides the login that is currently working for you, and the
#        error you get back does not say that is what happened.
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
